===Lady Luck===
Visit the south-central house and speak to the woman inside. She would like to visit [[Slateport City]] to purchase some [[Harbor Mail]], but has no bicycle for the long trip. Buy a piece of Mail from the Poké Mart there, then deliver it to her to receive a [[Coin Case]] as thanks. This case allows the holder to try their luck in the [[Mauville Game Corner]] and can hold up to 9,999 [[Coin (Game Corner)|Coins]], which may be redeemed for valuable prizes.

===A Smash Hit===
Visit the southeast house and speak to the Scientist inside to receive {{HM|06|Rock Smash}}. When used in the field, this move allows you to remove [[breakable rock]]s, often clearing the way to new areas in the process. Wild Pokémon may even appear when their hiding place is removed! To use it, Trainers must first earn the Badge from the local Gym.

===Rydel's Cycles===
A bicycle shop known as [[Rydel's Cycles]] is located in the northeast part of the city. [[Rydel|The owner]] notices how dirty your [[Running Shoes]] have become, and is shocked to learn that you have traveled all the way from [[Littleroot Town]] on foot. He decides to give you one of his bicycles, and explains that there are two different models available. The [[Mach Bike]] can reach speeds high enough to ride up {{DL|Bike obstacles|Muddy slopes|muddy slopes}} and over {{DL|Bike obstacles|Cracked tiles|cracked tiles}}. The [[Acro Bike]] can perform tricks, like wheelies and bunny hops. Each model allows the rider to reach areas that are otherwise inaccessible. Handbooks that explain each model's abilities are located in the store's backroom. Whichever model is selected may be exchanged for the other at any time by speaking to Rydel.
[[File:Mauville Game Corner interior RSE.png|thumb|Mauville Game Corner]]
===Mauville Game Corner===
The [[Mauville Game Corner]] is located in the southwest part of the city. The venue features two roulette wheels and sixteen slot machines. Coins can be purchased at the counter from the woman on the left in bundles of 50 for {{pdollar}}1,000 or 500 for {{pdollar}}10,000.

====Share the Wealth====
Speak to the girl to the left of the service counter. It turns out that she accidentally got two of the same Doll, and offers you the spare. The type of Doll received matches your [[first partner Pokémon]]: either a {{DL|List of decorations in Generation III|Treecko Doll}}, {{DL|List of decorations in Generation III|Torchic Doll}}, or {{DL|List of decorations in Generation III|Mudkip Doll}}.

====Prize Corner====
Coins can be exchanged for prizes at the counter from the two women on the right.

