The [[Mauville Gym]] specializes in {{type|Electric}} Pokémon. Electric-type [[move]]s are super effective against {{t|Flying}}- and {{type|Water}} {{OBP|Pokémon|species}}, while Electric-type Pokémon are weak to {{type|Ground}} moves.

The Gym features two sets of electrical barriers, one red and one blue, that can be toggled by stepping on floor switches that are shaped like a lightning bolt. Step on the switch nearest the door to disable the blue barriers and enable the red ones, then go east and fight Battle Girl Vivian. Step on the switch next to her to reactivate the blue barriers, then move southwest toward Youngster Ben. Go north and step on the final switch to reactivate the red barriers, then battle Guitarist Kirk to clear the way to the [[Gym Leader]].

[[Wattson]]'s {{p|Magnemite}} has a high {{stat|Special Attack}} rating, which lets it deal a good bit of damage with {{m|Thunder Shock|ThunderShock}}. {{m|Supersonic}} and {{m|Thunder Wave}} allow it to further harass the target with {{status|confusion}} and {{status|paralysis}}, respectively. {{p|Voltorb}}'s high {{stat|Speed}} can be problematic, especially if the volatile Pokémon decides to use {{m|Selfdestruct}}! His {{p|Magneton}} is similar to Magnemite, but {{m|Shock Wave}} is stronger than ThunderShock and never misses its target. {{type|Ground}} moves are effective against all three of Wattson's Pokémon, while Magnemite and Magneton are also vulnerable to {{t|Fire}} and {{t|Fighting}} attacks.

