===Pokémon Day Care===
The [[Pokémon Day Care]] is a facility that raises Pokémon for busy Trainers. For a small fee, up to two Pokémon can be left here to be raised by the Day Care staff. During their stay, Pokémon will gradually level up and learn new moves. When two {{DL|Pokémon breeding|How to breed|compatible}} Pokémon are left at the same time, their Trainer may return to find an [[Pokémon Egg|Egg]]! The two Pokémon must be of opposite genders, and the resulting Egg will hatch into the unevolved form of the female parent. The [[Day-Care Man]] watches over the Pokémon in their care from a gap in the fence, and hints at {{DL|Pokémon breeding|Breeding rate|the odds of finding one}}.

