===In Search of Sight===
From the east end of the tunnel, take the path on the left first. This leads to a secluded part of {{rt|116|Hoenn}} that was inaccessible on the previous visit. A PokéManiac here has lost his glasses, so dig out the [[Itemfinder]] to start searching. A pair of [[Black Glasses|BlackGlasses]] can be found a few steps west of him, but after inspection, he determines that they are not the pair that he lost. He wonders aloud if he even lost them in the area and wanders off to continue his search, leaving the BlackGlasses with you.

Before moving on, be sure to grab the [[HP Up]] from the mountainside.

===A Long-Awaited Reunion===
Follow the tunnel northward to find [[Wanda]] standing next to a pair of cracked rocks. Use {{m|Rock Smash}} to clear the debris, reuniting her with her hardworking boyfriend. He gives you {{HM|04|Strength}} as thanks, and the pair leave for her home so that he can rest. With the debris removed, the tunnel can now be used as a shortcut between western and central [[Hoenn]].

==Route 116==
===The Researcher's Reward===
Continue through Rusturf Tunnel to its western exit to return to {{rt|116|Hoenn}}. The same Devon researcher from earlier can be found just outside the tunnel. As thanks for delivering the [[Devon Parts|Devon Goods]] to [[Captain Stern]], he wishes to reward you with one of Devon's newest products: a [[Repeat Ball]]. From this point onward, Repeat Balls and [[Timer Ball]]s are available for purchase in [[Rustboro City]].



